            {
              "content": "=Role: You are a LaTeX Resume Expert and Career Consultant.\n\nTask: Optimize my LaTeX resume based on the provided \"Description\" and \"Judgement\" JSON feedback.\n\nStrict Rules for Editing:\n\nProfessional Summary: Rewrite this section to align with the \"Key Matches\" and \"Reasoning\" provided in the JSON.\n\nSkills Section: - Reorder the skills to prioritize those listed in \"Key Matches\" (e.g., Python, SQL, AWS, RAG).\n\nAdd any skills to the list that appear in my experience bullet points but were missing from the Skills section.\n\nExperience Bullet Points: - Reorder bullet points within each job to put the most relevant ones (based on the \"Key Matches\") at the top.\n\nRemove bullet points that are irrelevant to the judge's criteria, but do not edit the wording of the remaining points.\n\nProjects Section:\n\nReduce the total number of projects from 6 down to the 2-3 most relevant projects based on the \"Key Matches\" (e.g., prioritize the AWS Race Visualizer or DalVacation Home if they match the \"Full-stack\" or \"Cloud\" requirements).\n\nReorder the bullet points within those projects for maximum impact, but do not edit the wording.\n\nFormatting: Remove all comments, Maintain the exact LaTeX structure, packages, and custom commands (e.g., \\resumeItem, \\resumeSubheading). Ensure the document compiles perfectly.",
